 "note": "RPCS3 Core 914 (Core 912 was built but never pinned; Core 913 was its 4-way witness): Core 911 plus diagnostics for the open questions, all off by default. REWINDBOX_CAPTURE_912: two bounded captures enabled per title on the test page and started by a request of the host when its in-game menu closes (that menu does not pause the emulation; the request is a write of Enabled to the capture setting of the running title, taken by rpcs3_ios_set_game_setting before its idle contract, loading and saving nothing): COREPROF PUTLLCTRACE912 (per SPU thread, up to 512 consecutive data-changing accurate PUTLLC with the lane read, asked and found, six outcomes, one time base; REWINDBOX_CAPTURE_914: an event is stored only by the capture it was prepared under, an event of an earlier capture is refused and counted) and COREPROF PPUPROF912 (PPU threads sampled for at most 5 s by 256-byte regions of the last indirect transfer, system call or reservation instruction). The stall dump lists the FIFO position and the main thread's semaphores first. levers627 gains digits 19 to 21. No lock, barrier, reservation result or wait changes. SPUThread.cpp, an SPU identity input, changes in the host body of do_putllc() only (plus one include): one exact alias per Core (912, 914) in JITCacheCompatibility.cmake (Core 627 procedure, audited), identities unchanged. Host bridge 8977315e (test page rows, one capture request per closing of the in-game menu); MoltenVK dependency of run 42733987255 (library d19d3a42). Built by the RPCS3 Core route (run 42736141716, attempt 1, source ce12d397; Apple host harnesses run 42736141716 on ce12d397). Verified offline on the downloaded artifacts with the repository verifier (pin_errors and bundle). Not measured on the iPhone; no FPS claim.",
